#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554682} :activity/id #uuid "9ef07479-9bd3-50f2-b4da-e02ee5217b48" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048554 :topic/id #uuid "a93bb5a8-5344-5f11-a0fd-45410668ecd6" :topic/math-academy-id 1984} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554672 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554623 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "003c768f-4220-5a83-901d-9287c7398508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553864} {:answer/id #uuid "189491e7-f8db-50dd-a6d1-6eeaca6515ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{e-2}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553914} {:answer/id #uuid "c65e5475-456e-5a45-8351-be33d7aba2f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554305} {:answer/id #uuid "d5390bff-ed73-5aab-86b6-9bd0d5dc8156" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554334} {:answer/id #uuid "f88cff99-c81a-54d6-be8d-ad3057aab4a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554407}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553864} :answer-field/id #uuid "d777c8fd-8f4e-5ca8-a5be-b50636868cd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554521}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d5913a4b-d974-52bc-82fc-74c4bb66f8ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-102710" :question/problem "Consider the surface ${e}^{xy}-{x}^{2}-2{z}^{2}=e-3.$ Given that $n=⟨a,b,c⟩$ is a non-zero normal vector to the surface at the point $(1,1,-1),$ what is the value of $\\frac{a-b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define  $f(x,y,z)={e}^{xy}-{x}^{2}-2{z}^{2}.$ Then, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=e-3.$  \n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(1,1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xy}-{x}^{2}-2{z}^{2})i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy}-{x}^{2}-2{z}^{2}))j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{xy}-{x}^{2}-2{z}^{2})k \\\\  & =(y{e}^{xy}-2x)i+(x{e}^{xy})j+(-4z)k \\\\ ∇f(1,1,-1) & =((1){e}^{(1)(1)}-2(1))\\text{ }i+(1){e}^{(1)(1)}\\text{ }j+(-4)(-1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(e-2)\\text{ }i+e\\text{ }j+4\\text{ }k \\\\  & =⟨e-2,\\,e,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩=⟨e-2,\\,e,\\,4⟩.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{a-b}{c}=\\frac{(e-2)-e}{4}=-\\frac{1}{2}.$"} :step/id #uuid "48086a64-8671-5a00-bbb5-b58661fd7a59" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554715}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554677 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366808 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9d90141-bb87-557b-8f42-7d42bba3c91d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x+2y+4z-16=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366810} {:answer/id #uuid "152ddd87-e22d-58da-85bb-b549e713fa60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x+4y+3z-10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366811} {:answer/id #uuid "e03a5aca-94df-508f-a37f-bf286cd93f47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x-3y+z-11=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366812} {:answer/id #uuid "e48a7bda-ef25-5ea3-836f-2a4b00051777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5x+y+2z-11=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366813} {:answer/id #uuid "c0b69228-be90-5f3b-83c0-2b8ff34eb2da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-2y+z-9=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366814}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366810} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab905e04-ebcb-5bbc-8e7d-cdb57e6bb24a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366809}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "843be179-016c-55ad-bf04-357dd9b69f33" :question/math-academy-id "q-102701" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=xyz-{z}^{2}$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes  through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,3,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(2,3,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyz-{z}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xyz-{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xyz-{z}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =yz\\text{ }i+xz\\text{ }j+(xy-2z)k \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,3,1) & =(3)(1)\\text{ }i+2(1)\\text{ }j+(2(3)-2(1))k \\\\  & =3\\,i+2\\,j+4k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(2,3,1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-3,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨3,2,4⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-3,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 3(x-2)+2(y-3)+4(z-1) & =0 \\\\ 3x+2y+4z-16 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "588c4361-50c9-5029-a566-867e8863cbe8" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554672}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554682 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394071 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55726bdf-bd92-5f7e-a7bc-7a1d0597e754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-3,2,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394073} {:answer/id #uuid "9575e423-448b-5b5c-91fc-c2a7c6afcec3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨2,-3,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394074} {:answer/id #uuid "21a4639b-6da9-5a98-9ba9-dde732cd477b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-3,2,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,\\,y+2,\\,z-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394075} {:answer/id #uuid "14d65a68-8209-56ec-85e3-86c5087733e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨2,-3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394076} {:answer/id #uuid "6fd689ee-da18-5ee8-8e2e-94f4eb0e8982" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨3,2,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394077}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394073} :answer-field/id #uuid "1883a36c-4cc8-545f-9348-6c077cb4b1e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6f18a33a-3190-5d7a-b7c8-c7f2c7cbfe22" :question/math-academy-id "q-80768" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}-xz$,  find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,-1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(2,-1,-1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}-xz)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}-xz)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}-xz)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(2xy-z)\\text{ }i+({x}^{2}+2y)\\text{ }j-xk \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,-1,-1) & =(\\,2(2)(-1)-(-1)\\,)\\text{ }i+(\\,{2}^{2}+2(-1)\\,)\\text{ }j-2k \\\\  & =-3\\,i+2\\,j-2\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-3,2,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(2,-1,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-3,2,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7191b9bd-5ed6-54dc-8494-3debf9947402" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554749}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554715 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554541 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "065677e5-6668-589c-8f82-28615b7c7eea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-6y+z-13=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553881} {:answer/id #uuid "8da732bc-eb58-5338-abe0-8d52e81e25e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x+8y-5z+12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554168} {:answer/id #uuid "bd87e438-6635-5fc8-8041-e85ff749d4dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-x+9y-z+16=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554281} {:answer/id #uuid "d50bfffc-a66c-5b56-a37e-a72964286f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x+5y-6z-3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554332} {:answer/id #uuid "ea005b66-1e1f-575c-a788-5fbfb346d025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-x+8y-6z+30=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554379}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554379} :answer-field/id #uuid "74e95cce-259a-58bc-a6dc-cf74c51c993b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554475}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "138bcf11-9efc-57ee-ad7b-ef21818db0e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-102712" :question/problem "Consider the surface ${z}^{2}y+16=4\\sqrt{x}+y.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to that surface at the point $(4,-1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}y+16 & =4\\sqrt{x}+y. \\\\ {z}^{2}y-4\\sqrt{x}-y & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)={z}^{2}y-4\\sqrt{x}-y$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=-16.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(4,-1,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({z}^{2}y-4\\sqrt{x}-y)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({z}^{2}y-4\\sqrt{x}-y)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2}y-4\\sqrt{x}-y)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}\\text{ }i+({z}^{2}-1)\\text{ }j+2zy\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(4,-1,3) & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4}}\\text{ }i+({3}^{2}-1)\\text{ }j+2(3)(-1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =-\\,i+8\\text{ }j-6\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-1,8,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(4,-1,3)\\cdot ⟨x-4,\\,y+1,\\,z-3⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-1,8,-6⟩\\cdot ⟨x-4,\\,y+1,\\,z-3⟩ & =0 \\\\ -(x-4)+8(y+1)-6(z-3) & =0 \\\\ -x+8y-6z+30 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9ee2cdbe-40de-5a18-809a-b2ba9fbc04a8"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554749 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554584 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1038e636-38ca-52da-90c5-a091da531eb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2ex+2ey+\\frac{z}{e}-4e+\\frac{1}{e}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553902} {:answer/id #uuid "27782ffe-f397-5d41-939c-10588c08a068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2ex-2ey-\\frac{z}{e}-\\frac{1}{e}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553943} {:answer/id #uuid "8605bb25-4120-54e0-870c-c12a2d8a2246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2ex+2ey+\\frac{z}{e}-2e+\\frac{1}{e}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554145} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a1e914-b611-51ed-ac80-498a071f0b9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2ex+2ey+ez+3e=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554262} {:answer/id #uuid "c1fe292e-1813-51b6-937f-ba4fbfabb74f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2ex+2ey-\\frac{z}{e}-4e-\\frac{1}{e}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554290}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554290} :answer-field/id #uuid "102d43bf-f5e9-5d2c-bd0c-f23bbb64ece6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554437}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6cd59b40-dc86-5174-9cba-78e6f66091cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-86454" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=2y{e}^{x}-{e}^{z}$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y{e}^{x}-{e}^{z})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y{e}^{x}-{e}^{z})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2y{e}^{x}-{e}^{z})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2y{e}^{x}\\text{ }i+2{e}^{x}\\text{ }j-{e}^{z}k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,1,-1) & =2(1)e\\text{ }i+2e\\text{ }j-{e}^{-1}k \\\\  & =2e\\,i+2e\\,j-{e}^{-1}k \\\\  & =⟨2e,2e,-\\frac{1}{e}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,1,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z+1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨2e,2e,-\\frac{1}{e}⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z+1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 2ex+2ey-\\frac{z}{e}-4e-\\frac{1}{e} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "fb365c06-0aef-539e-aff8-8e2d2bf57273" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554677}}] :activity/title "Tangent Planes to Level Surfaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553851}]}
